        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">The Life Fitness Club Series+ is a club-built treadmill that fits a
          home: a 4.0 HP continuous AC motor, a 22 by 60-inch deck, lifetime frame and motor cover and a
          standard 15-amp outlet, from $6,079 with the SL console at Life Fitness on 5 November 2026.</strong>
          The SE4 adds a 24-inch touchscreen, classes and Lifescape courses for $8,799 in the same sale.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the SL unless the SE4's content is the reason you want it, and compare it honestly with the
          <a href="/life-fitness-run-cx-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Run CX</a>,
          which matches its deck, speed, incline and user rating for much less. Choose the Club Series+
          when several people will run on it often, and get the price, lead time and warranty in writing
          from your seller.
          </p>
